                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bad7e45b-d831-3171-ad76-a4c45c779442",
                        "entry_id": "403d1268-5cc6-3a28-b27b-4355f708a8b3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Assyrian (related to Assyria, ancient region on the Upper Tigris river)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "03d911b6-d5c1-410d-8980-b182802f0299",
                                "sense_id": "bad7e45b-d831-3171-ad76-a4c45c779442",
                                "text": "Ассирийский царь Асархадон завоевал царство царя Лаилиэ, разорил и сжёг все города, жителей всех перегнал в свою землю, воинов перебил, самого же царя Лаилиэ посадил в клетку.",
                                "translation": "The Assyrian King, Esarhaddon, had conquered the kingdom of King Lailie, had destroyed and burnt the towns, taken all the inhabitants captive to his own country, slaughtered the warriors, beheaded some chieftains and impaled or flayed others, and had confined King Lailie himself in a cage.",
                                "english": "The Assyrian King, Esarhaddon, had conquered the kingdom of King Lailie, had destroyed and burnt the towns, taken all the inhabitants captive to his own country, slaughtered the warriors, beheaded some chieftains and impaled or flayed others, and had confined King Lailie himself in a cage."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
